# Historical session launch prompts — September 7, 2026

The former three-peer launch plan (`msc-context`, `msc-migration`,
`msc-authoring`) is retired. Its read-only first checkpoint and instruction to
wait for resumption belonged to that launch; they do not govern later work.
The full prompts are recoverable with:

```bash
git show 774c3286:docs/session-briefs.md
```

Use [current work](../memories/todos.md) for assignments. Useful findings and
rationale from that planning work have these owners:

- [Planning context](../memories/planning-context.md): user corrections,
  authoring expectations, deferred summary design and limits of retrieval trials.
- [Architecture migration](../memories/architecture-migration.md): concrete
  code candidates, consumers, semantic differences and proposed checks.
- [Outcome coverage](../memories/outcome-coverage.md): omitted composition,
  proof and delivery work, plus bounded source discoveries.
- [Authoring evidence](../memories/authoring-workflow.md) and
  [data-science evidence](../memories/datascience-scope.md): findings for those domains.
- [Former portfolio](../memories/team-plan.md): execution-reliability leads
  and rationale retained from the superseded five-peer proposal.

The old prompts also recorded an unauthorized expensive table rebuild. Its
cost and reproduction limits are retained in [migration review](migration-review.md).
Old host/sandbox and shared-skill paths are historical; current setup belongs
in [INSTALL.md](../INSTALL.md), not a launch prompt.
